#!/usr/bin/env bash

lord --verbose << "EOF"

1. Fix all the font warnings like this:

LaTeX Font Warning: Font shape `TU/paleo-hebrew-tel-dan.ttf(0)/b/n' undefined
(Font)              using `TU/paleo-hebrew-tel-dan.ttf(0)/m/n' instead on input
 line 2101.

2. Fix the incorrect Levite Mushite highlighting on the 'key to sources' page
in the italics section that causes too much stuff to be yellow and then bleeds
into the footnotes.

3. The word 'background' is there twice on the key to sources page. Remove the
green one from the background section.

4. 'Redactors. Editors, occasionally'... should be 'Redactors, Editors. Occasionally'...
on the same page.

5. Remove Records and Other from the header (but not the body) on the same page.

6. Unbold P's Hebrew font. I know he's a Levite and that's how it should work,
but P's Hebrew is already bold enough. Can we fix this at the font loading step?
It applies to all \Levite's who use that font, which also includes R, so at the
Ezra font load step it would be best to fix it there.

7. P's blue needs to be a bit darker in dark mode, it's a little too soothing,
and P's a threating sort of guy, so it should be darker.

8. The footnotes here need % on the line before them to prevent the space

And there’s still no land. 5
Also the day ends before he got a chance to say “it was good.” 6

9. R's background needs to be *slightly* more visible in dark mode.
Not sure what the best way to do that is, but consider the aesthetics
carefully before you do.

10. You messed up the \redacted color in dark mode when you made master.tex,
it's better in old/main.tex, unless you changed it there, in which case
look through the git history and find the brighter darker version.
It should be the same color as Rcolor in light mode if I'm not mistaken,
even though that feels a bit inconsistent, it's needed for visibility
and intensity.

11. 'Translator's Aside' around Genesis 1:21/1:22 should be a footnote, but
it popped out of footnote mode somehow. Fix that. It should be a hangingfootnote
or whatever we called those, there's a function for it.

12. R should have niqqud too, but keep RJE without them.

13. In Genesis 2:7 where you see me highlighting hebrew and english *bible*
text with red and blue, I want you to write \\hlA, \\hlB, and \\hlC functions
that will *highlight* by adding as a background color the foreground color of
the commentary characters A, B, and C. B is always red, C is always blue, but
A is black in light mode and white in dark mode. The highlight functions should
preserve the foreground colors, and you should replace all \\cK in bible text
with \\hlA, all \\cR with \\hlB, and all \\cB with \\hlC. Only in bible text,
english or hebrew, in [12345]-* dirs. Don't make those replacements in commentary
text.

14. Use Paleo Hebrew Standard font for E.

15. Add a source PaleoP, we'll call it PP for short. Keep P as is, but if we occasionally
want to point out that P *would have* probably written in Paleo Hebrew since he
wrote around the time of Hezekiah, then we can switch to PP with some simple
\renewcommand or something. Add support for this, summarize the gist in the source fonts
page P section at the beginning of the book, and then add a comment somewhere noticeable
saying how to switch to PaleoP and then back to SquareP.
EOF
